WEBVTT

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:35.340
Lakeview to Bennett. Lakeview to Bennett.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:38.760
- Did you get him? - No, I haven't had him for an hour.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:52.450
Lakeview to Bennett.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:57.360
It's all right, darling. We'll be there soon, now.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:10.850
to Bennett. Lakeview to Bennett. Lakeview to Bennett. Oh, I ain't so worried. Anything

00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:16.040
Dick Bennett can fly, he can land. He can't land. We have a ceiling of 300 and a visibility

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:20.740
of about six inches. Out in a storm with a sick baby on board. Well, Dick's that kind

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:24.450
of a guy. There ain't another guy who can make it. He hasn't made a chance. Oh, he's been

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:30.000
in tougher spots than this. You know that. I ain't worried. Any guy that makes a late

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:32.770
I've got sense enough to be worried.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:43.720
Bennett to Lakeview. Bennett to Lakeview.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:47.800
Lakeview to Bennett. Bennett? Go ahead, Bennett.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:51.290
Coming in.

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:54.720
You can't come in. Ceiling 300, visibility one-eighth of a mile.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:57.610
Move over to Port Dover.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.890
Short of gas, and a lamp.

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:04.920
- It's like soup down here, Bennett. Keep on the other field. - I'm coming through.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:14.180
Get out the crash car.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.120
Put this on.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:53.520
Take care of yourself, honey.

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:09.890
I don't know how to thank you forget it. Good luck to the little girl. You big phone. No, you scared us today

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:15.150
Better check up on those motors. They're burning too much gas. All right. Hey, I've got a great idea for that new plane of yours

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:28.170
Come on you need some coffee. Hey, how about some service? What do you got to eat? I'm coming. We got distinguished company

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:30.000
Don't tell me it's the great

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.900
- Mr. Bennett. - Hello, Mary.

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:33.900
- Hello, what do you have? - Coffee.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:36.160
- Me too, and don't forget... - The cream.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.830
- Right. Boy, you had me scared to death.

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:41.430
From now on, there'll be no more flying left

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:42.630
of the Stanley Cup races.

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:44.220
We're taking no chances.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:45.700
- Do you really think the plane is ready?

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:46.740
- I know it is.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:49.860
Gee, this is what we've been dreaming about for years.

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:51.540
You flying the ship that I built.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:53.180
- You've got a lot of money into it, Bill.

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:54.590
- Now, don't worry about that.

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:56.710
Well, we got three standing offers for the plans.

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:58.130
If we win, we're all set.

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.000
- How does the competition look?

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.450
Way till you get a load of the competition parked in our hangar.

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:04.270
What do you mean?

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:06.470
Oh, a dame barged in with a ship today.

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:09.120
I'm telling you, she's got everything on there but a calliope.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.020
You know, one of those Miss Millions out looking for a thrill?

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:15.300
Why, at the field, they've practically laid out a red plush carpet for us.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:16.160
Who built the plane?

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:18.160
Oh, I don't know. It's some sort of a foreign thing.

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:21.690
You know, the American era slogan, "Made in America, Spent in Europe"?

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:22.490
Way till you see it.

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:24.690
Why, she's got gold knobs on the controls.

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:26.490
With lace curtains on the windows?

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:29.590
I got ten bucks that she looks like a ham sandwich.

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:33.850
Hey, buddy, pass the sugar.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:44.030
What was the idea of that?

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:46.730
Compliments from the ham sandwich.

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:51.070
Ham sandwich, eh?

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:53.140
I'll take that $10 bet.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:55.460
Let me have a napkin, Mary.

00:05:57.340 --> 00:05:57.700
Nothing.

00:05:57.980 --> 00:05:58.900
And a fresh cup of coffee.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:00.000
I said I'd take that.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.900
Hey, Carter wants us to go over to the hangar tomorrow and take a look at those two ships he's going to sell to the Russians.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:06.820
You're not trying to change the subject, are you?

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:11.000
I said Carter wants us to come over to the hangar tomorrow and look at those two ships he's going to sell to the Russians.

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:13.640
Okay, we'll go over to the hangar tomorrow and look at those ships.

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:15.980
Looks like you're going over to the hangar and look at some ships.

00:06:17.590 --> 00:06:19.650
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha.

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:35.290
- Well, Dick, what do you think of it?

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:36.410
- Carter, she's a pippin'.

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:39.400
You've got things on there I've never seen in a plane before.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:40.400
- Would you like to fly it?

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:41.480
- I sure would.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:42.320
- Why can't you?

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:44.360
Can you get out of your contract with Consolidated?

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:47.000
- No, I have to fly that transport for the next six months.

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:48.250
- I'll say he does.

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:49.710
Right, they took the President of the United States

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:51.090
to get permission for him to fly our ship

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:52.580
in the Stanley Trophy race.

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:53.520
- Well, how's it coming?

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:55.370
- Fastest thing around.

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:57.000
With this guy in the cockpit.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:57.960
Say, we gotta get back there.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:06:58.760
- Yeah.

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:00.000
Thanks, Carter, for the offer.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:00.920
Well, think it over.

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:04.760
I'm giving a little informal party night for the boys up in my place.

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:07.240
Sort of a send-off before the races.

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:09.580
I'll expect you boys up.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:10.930
Thanks, but...

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:11.450
We'll be there.

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:12.860
So long.

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:13.760
So long, Carter.

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:14.380
So long.

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:26.800
When?

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:27.640
Too much fog.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:29.870
Oh, I got some over here to fix that fog.

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:30.000
Oh, I got some over here to fix that fog.

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:31.810
Well, hello, Major. Glad to see you.

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:33.250
Edwards, I'm glad to see you again.

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:35.150
Major, I'd like you to know Dick Bennett.

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:36.350
How do you do, Major?

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:39.180
Pleasure, Mr. Bennett. It's a pleasure, I'm sure.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:40.310
Uh, what do you have?

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:41.510
Oh, scotch and soda, please.

00:07:41.510 --> 00:07:42.610
I don't care for anything, thank you.

00:07:42.610 --> 00:07:44.650
Uh, bring me a glass of water, please.

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:45.750
Edwards, I ever took you...

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:47.050
Uh, yes, Major. Uh, you did.

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:49.070
I did. Oh, yes, right. Yes, you did.

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:50.470
